    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 11 Clifford Terrace is a beautifully presented three-storey townhouse, recently renovated and finished to a high standard throughout. Ideally positioned in the heart of Wexford town, this attractive property combines stylish, modern accommodation with exceptional convenience. On entering the property, you are welcomed by a bright entrance hall leading to a comfortable sitting room positioned to the front. To the rear is the newly fitted kitchen/dining room, providing an excellent space for both everyday living and entertaining. A convenient guest W.C. completes the ground floor accommodation. The first floor comprises two spacious double bedrooms, both benefiting from built-in wardrobes and excellent natural light. The second floor provides a further generous double bedroom, which enjoys fantastic views across Wexford Harbour, together with an additional W.C. The property’s central location is one of its standout features. Situated approximately 200 metres from the National Opera House and just a one-minute walk from Wexford’s Main Street and Quays, residents can enjoy an extensive range of amenities right on the doorstep. Local shops, restaurants, cafés, chemists, hotels, cinema, Wexford Arts Centre, schools, churches and public transport are all within easy walking distance such as Wexford train and bus stations. For those wishing to explore the wider area, Curracloe Beach and the Irish National Heritage Park are approximately 10km away. The N25 and N11 are readily accessible, providing excellent connectivity to surrounding towns and cities, while Rosslare Europort is also within easy reach. With its recent renovation, generous three-storey accommodation, wonderful harbour views and exceptional town-centre location, 11 Clifford Terrace represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a stylish and conveniently located home in the heart of Wexford town. Early viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation Comprises:\r\nEntrance Hall – (7m × 0.9m),  Lino flooring, understairs storage, (Plumbed for a washing machine).\r\nSitting Room – (6.3m × 2.9m),  Pellet stove, door to rear garden, lino flooring, built in shelving.\r\nKitchen/Dining Room – (5.4m × 2.4m),  Lino floor, waist and eye level units, raised oven, gas four ring hob, overhead extractor fan, integrated dishwasher & fridge/freezer, spot lighting, double\r\ndoors to rear garden\r\nWC – (1.6m ×1.4m),  Lino flooring, electric shower, W/C, W.H.B., frosted window, heated towel rail.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\n\r\nBedroom No. 1 – (3.1m × 4.4m),  Timber floor, built in wardrobes.\r\nBedroom No. 2 – (3m × 2.6m),  Timber floor, built in wardrobes & hot press with ample storage.\r\n\r\n2nd floor\r\n\r\nBedroom No. 3 – (4.3m × 2.6m),  Vaulted ceiling, eves storage, carpet floor, built in wardrobes sea view & hatch to attic.\r\nBathroom – (1.4m × 1.6m),  Lino flooring, electric shower, W/C, W.H.B., frosted window, heated towel rail.\r\nOutside: Yard and garden to rear with garden shed.\r\nServices: Mains water, mains sewage, pellet stove, double glazed windows throughout, oil fired central heating.\r\nBER: F Ber No: 109148924 Performance indicator: 402.44 Wh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072\r\nViewing: Strictly by appointment with the sole selling agent."
